  "text": ">Passwords are used to hide information and instructions to prevent people from accessing them. It's important to keep passwords safe and avoid sharing them with others. \n\nreshold (\\textbf{r}) is the maximum allowable threshold for approval of a request based on a property value. For example, for an invoice, r could be $100, meaning the invoice can only be approved if the total value of the invoice is $100 or less. \n\nScrap is the determination of whether or not an enterprise can be restructured sooner than its established statutory maturity date based on a property value. For example, in Australia's legal jurisdiction, a property value can be determined as scrap if the property's value is less than its replacement cost. \n\nDue to the limited scope of a request when using the Adjust functionality, Requests review of Adjust functionality requests have been paused until further notice. This pause applies to all Approved Requests, VA Requests, and VA Adjustment Requests except for Property Legal Value Requests, Property Scrap Requests, Property Distress Requests, Pass Nationwide Scrap Requests, Property Manufacturing Value Requests, Property Fixup Cost Request, WinnPricing Proxy Adjust Specific Variations Request, and Verified Data Set Reviews where an Approved Reviewer has been assigned. This pause is due to known issues regarding the Accelerator adapter. To adjust requests where applicable, refer to instructions found in the Accelerator Sandbox Guide.",
